      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "In a typical synthesis, a methanol solution (5 mL) of Yb(ClO4)3·6H2O (0.058 g, 0.1 mmol) was added to a dichloromethane solution (20 mL) of H2L (0.068 g, 0.2 mmol). The mixture was stirred for 10 h at ambient temperature, filtered, and hexane was slowly diffused into the filtrate. The solution was stored in the dark at ambient temperature, giving yellow crystals in about two weeks. Complexes 1–5 are described as prepared by similar procedures (Scheme S1); crystals of 1 were grown by solvent diffusion.",
